Z||000018||rogergarrison||10-23-2001||03:25 PM||||I can buy real ones for $15k-$20 from my dealer sources. The problem is like  been said a million times here, the maintainence is way outta line and I drive the hell out of mine (90,000 in less than 4 years). with normal routine maintainence on the real one in the same miles id have spent another $25K since I got it and for example $3500.00 for the clutch replacement, muffler is almost $1,000 more. The real cherry on top is I have smoked 2 'real' 308's on the hiway, much to their embarrassment. And as for fiberglass, real 308's from 76-77 were also fiberglass. When the real one breaks down in the boonies with a $10.00 part, he has it towed 200 miles, waits for 2 months, pays $1,000 to have it installed....I go to autozone. all that any 95% of people see me driving down the road dont know the differnce anyway.||||reg||1
